{"id": "8ff50e1f-37f4-4b1d-a0de-a0b8384c2036", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check the Bedrock quotas that apply in us-east-1, both default and applied values. I'll also look at your recent throttling metrics to see which models are being hit and how close you run to the limits.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_9hFVw0hoChW96koiCuFo0D", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-quota-check", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["exploring-metrics", "verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Determine the actual effective Amazon Bedrock runtime quotas in us-east-1 and how they relate to observed throttling.",
  "context": "User says they are throttled on Bedrock in us-east-1 during business hours and that they NEVER requested a quota increase. They want to know their actual limit and what to do. Keep this a focused, shallow pass.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1 (agent space account; check other associated accounts only if list_associations shows Bedrock-using ones)", "region us-east-1", "Service Quotas service code: bedrock", "CloudWatch namespace AWS/Bedrock (InvocationThrottles, Invocations, InputTokenCount, OutputTokenCount, dimension ModelId)"],
  "timeframe": "last 7 days up to 2026-11-24T18:50:00Z, focusing on business hours (roughly 13:00-22:00 UTC)",
  "criteria": "1) Via Service Quotas list the Bedrock quotas for on-demand InvokeModel/Converse requests-per-minute and tokens-per-minute for the models that are actually being used (identify them from the CloudWatch metrics first rather than dumping all quotas). For each report: quota name, quota code, applied value, AWS default value, whether adjustable, and whether an applied (account-level) override exists. Note whether cross-region inference profile quotas differ from the in-region model quotas. 2) From CloudWatch, report per ModelId: peak invocations per minute, peak tokens per minute (input+output; note output tokens are burndown-weighted for some models), throttle counts and when they cluster. 3) Compare peak usage to the quota to say if throttling is plausibly quota-driven. 4) Check docs briefly for current guidance on throttling (ThrottlingException), cross-region inference profiles, provisioned throughput, and quota increase process. Do NOT make any changes. Return a concise summary with a table of model / applied quota / default / peak usage / throttles, and flag anything you could not determine."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check Bedrock quotas and throttling metrics in us-east-1"}], "created_at": null}

